    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d435-a3">

                <pb facs="0667" n="593" xml:id="pg593"/>

                <head>[Special despatch to the World.]</head>

                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-01-05"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >January</hi> 5, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>This morning the Peruvian minister and an officer of the Peruvian navy visited
                    the splendid monitor Miantonomoh, now at the navy yard, for the purpose of
                    inspecting it. The Peruvian government has already one double-turretted monitor,
                    and her neighbor, Chili, has two, being built in England, and the minister from
                    Peru is anxious to purchase one of our monitors for his government.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
